{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793641942,"nonce":"EtTLAYxmF9ACrsZ2CC7le03X8sQ=","title":"print and console.log write(2) once per line even to files and pipes","message":"plugins/zrtl_io/src/lib.rs uses print!/println!, and Rust stdout is always a LineWriter: a write(2) per newline plus the stdout lock per piece. TS runtime (zyntax_ts/src/runtime.rs print_number, print_space, print_newline) and zylua host_io Inner::Stdout write_all do the same.\n\nRepro: for i in range(300000): print(i) redirected to a file: about 490 ms zypy, 88 ms CPython, 40 ms PyPy. Lua for i=1,300000 do print(i) end: about 500 ms zylua, 21 ms LuaJIT.\n\nDirection: process-wide block-buffered writer when stdout is not a tty, flushed at exit, before stdin reads and around stderr writes.","files":null}]}